---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CtaPanel from '../components/CtaPanel.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.js';
---
<Layout
  title="Inspection Repairs & Contractor Help for Real Estate Agents | Upkeep"
  description="A reliable repair partner for Middle Tennessee real estate agents. Inspection report repairs, pre-listing punch lists, and flat-rate quotes your clients can trust, on closing timelines."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">For Real Estate Agents</span>
      <h1>The contractor your rolodex is missing.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Every agent has lost sleep over an inspection report two weeks before
        closing. The repair list is in hand, the deadline is real, and every
        contractor in your phone is booked, unlicensed, or not answering.
        Upkeep is the maintenance partner agents keep for exactly that moment.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-ctas">
        <a href="/work-order/" class="btn btn-primary">Send Us a Repair List</a>
        <a href={site.phoneHref} class="btn btn-ghost">Call {site.phone}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What we handle for agents</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Inspection report repairs</h3>
          <p>Send the inspection report and we quote the repair items flat, line by line. Your client sees a real number fast, and the work gets documented with photos for the repair amendment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Pre-listing punch lists</h3>
          <p>The small stuff that costs sellers money in negotiations: caulk, paint touch-ups, loose fixtures, sticking doors. One visit before photos, and the listing shows like it should.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Closing-deadline scheduling</h3>
          <p>Repair timelines in a contract are not suggestions. We schedule against your closing date and confirm completion with photos you can forward to the other side.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Twelve trades, one call</h3>
          <p>Inspection lists cross trades by nature: a little electrical, a little plumbing, some rot, some paint. One crew handles the whole list instead of four subcontractors handling a quarter each.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Documentation for the file</h3>
          <p>Photo reports and itemized invoices for every job, so the repair receipt your client hands over at closing actually holds up.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>A partner for your clients after closing</h3>
          <p>Buyers ask agents for contractor referrals for years after the sale. Be the agent whose referral answers the phone.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>Why agents keep us in the rolodex</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          We are investors ourselves, so we work on transaction timelines
          constantly and we know a delayed repair can delay a closing. You get
          a confirmed request within two business hours, a flat quote your
          client can approve without fear, and finished work with proof.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>How to work with us</h2>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li>Email or submit the inspection report or repair addendum</li>
          <li>We return a flat-rate, line-item quote</li>
          <li>Your client approves, we schedule against the closing date</li>
          <li>Photos and an itemized invoice close out the file</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top: 16px;">
          Read more: <a href="/articles/inspection-repairs-for-real-estate-agents/">why every agent needs a repair partner in their rolodex</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaPanel
    heading="Have an inspection report on your desk?"
    body="Send it over today and we will have a line-item quote back to keep your closing on schedule."
  />
</Layout>
